# This mod ships no assembly and has nothing to build, so the compilation rules below are
# inherited convention rather than a live need. The entry that earns its place here is
# .claude/: a session worktree is a full copy of the monorepo, hundreds of megabytes, and it
# has already landed inside a mod folder once.
#
# Two separate reasons to have this file, and only the first is about git:
#
#   - The monorepo's own .gitignore covers all of this, but `git subtree split` exports this
#     folder alone. The root's rules do not travel with it.
#   - Steam does not read .gitignore at all. SteamUGC.SetItemContent takes the junction's
#     target directory as it stands on disk, with no filtering, so anything sitting in the
#     published folder is published. That is what `Mod/` is for: the junction points there,
#     and everything else in this folder - Art/, the docs, this file - stays out of reach by
#     construction.

# Build intermediates.
.build/
Source/obj/
Source/bin/

# Claude Code session worktrees and local settings: each worktree is a full copy of the
# monorepo, and they are never shared.
.claude/

# Showcase notes: French working notes, deleted once Preview.png and ModIcon.png are done.
PROMPT_*.md

# Development environments.
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.csproj.user

# System.
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Generated DDS copies of the textures. Each has a tracked .png twin in the same folder, which is
# what the game loads, so the .dds add nothing to the source. Eight of them sat in Mod/ when the
# 0.1.0 prepublication of 2026-09-23 was uploaded; they never were tracked, and this keeps them
# from ever being committed. They stay on disk locally.
*.dds

# Test evidence lives on disk and is ignored. The record that is versioned is the text summary in
# docs/runs/. What to keep, and how to cut it down, is written in docs/runs/README.md.
Tests/Pickle/evidence/
Tests/Manual/evidence/
evidence/

# Raw captures of another author's Steam page and of its comment thread, kept on disk as the dated
# proof behind the `silent` licence decision. They hold other people's names and words, so they do
# not go into a public repository; the summary next to them, README.md, does.
Audit/*/steam-page.html
Audit/*/steam-comments.json
